{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/768285-ex3-help-me-make-a-solar-smooth-criminal","id":768285,"title":"[EX3] Help me make a Solar Smooth Criminal!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-17T22:04:35-08:00","id":768285,"title":"[EX3] Help me make a Solar Smooth Criminal!","content":"So, been trying to mak characters for a while now for Ex 3, but uh... honestly having a bit of trouble for most non-combat Charms, how they relate to the game system and such. So asking for help of those who might have a better overview.<br /> <br /> I want to make a Night Caste Master Criminal, with Supernal Larceny. The idea is to make Ezekiel Jones from the Librarians, or someone from Leverage. People who will say with a straight face &quot;Let's go steal a satrapy/god/yeddim&quot;. <br /> <br /> Wass thinking of decking him out with Awareness, Investigation, Dodge, Stealth and Socialize as well. For combat not sure... he would be more of a parkour using non-combatant, though I guess he can take a Martial Art... black claw, crane or Dreaming Pearl perhaps :P<br /> <br /> No idea on merits.<br /> <br /> So, any reccommendations what would be the best way to make this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T22:12:45-08:00","id":768287,"title":"","content":"Supernal Larceny is a good go... If you're going to have a lot of stealth, investing in Ebon Shadow Style might synergize well...<br /> <br /> For Merits there's things like Danger Sense. And Contacts or Allies will be handy, if you want to keep his ear to the ground with regards to what's going on in the city. Some decent Resources, naturally.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, and if he's not going to be Melee-focused, yeah, DODGE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 11-18-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T08:35:35-08:00","id":768531,"title":"","content":"Null Anima Gloves (10 Charms total) and Fate Shifting Arete (x2) (Another four charms on top of Null Anima Gloves) are the big heavy lifters in Larceny, though you don't need to start with Fate Shifting Arete. You will do just fine with in Combat with Null Anima Gloves and a decent combat skill to hit with Decisives. I would start with Null Anima Gloves and Ox-Body (x2 or ideally x3). I am going to recommend you use either Sorcery or Martial Arts as your combat ability so you can buy those up with Solar EXP. Sorcery requires a <i>much</i> smaller investment for what is arguably a bigger effect.<br /> <br /> In order to steal a Yeddim you are going to need Athletics Charms. Particularly Thunderer's Might.<br /> In order to steal a God you are going to need Sorcery, Integrity, or and/or Occult Charms.<br /> In order to steal a Satrapy you are going to need Socialize, Bureaucracy Charms and probably War.<br /> * Your Circlemates can probably take care of some of that.<br /> <br /> For Merits...<br /> Contacts are highly appropriate.<br /> Followers are appropriate if you are leading an organization.<br /> Backing is appropriate if you are a member of a bigger organization.<br /> Resources to represent your life of crime.<br /> Mighty Threw to help with pickpocketing Yeddims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 11-18-2015, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T13:02:37-08:00","id":768685,"title":"","content":"Thanks all, nice ideas.<br /> <br /> My idea is coming together, especially background-wise:<br /> <br /> [Witty Name] was born the son of a renowned courtesan of the Realm. His mother's status allowed him not to be thrown into one of the orphanages, but to be raised at her work place. There he learned important lessons (children must be heard, but not seen. Or not heard really. Also, rich and drunk people can give you expensive things. Also also, ladies must be treated nicely. They work for it.). Despite his skill, he wass a troublesome child who was always more that could be handled. One day, when he was but a wee tween, he escaped after his mother's latest admonishment (Do Not Seduce the Ragara Heir, how many times do I have to tell you?!). <br /> <br /> Ever since then, he was on the road, earning money via pick pocketing, lying, and general (but classy!) skullduggery. Also, he Exalted when stealing an Immaculate Sacred Scrol once. Fun times.<br /> <br /> Skill-wise:<br /> Supernal Larceny, because that is who he is<br /> Awareness, because noticing things is good for someone who lies for a living<br /> Investigation, because when you've done so many crimes, you kinda pick up on their details<br /> Stealth, because heard but not seen. Also not heard.<br /> Dodge, because being hit in the face is bad, m'kay?<br /> Linguistics because writing is useful. So is forgery!<br /> Athletics, because not being hit is fun. Also parkour<br /> <br /> Also, Yeddim stealing can be done via the forgery of all official paperwork! (Yes, the Guild has requested the transfer of this Yeddim in particular. Yes, him. CAN YOU NOT READ THE SEAL?!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T13:58:27-08:00","id":768712,"title":"","content":"[Witty Name] should be named like... &quot;Endless Wit&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> Also, while I initially thought about Ebon Shadow Style, you might be able to get by with a LOT of bluffing, guile, fast-talking, and maybe some Thrown if they're onto you.<br /> <br /> I noticed that you still have room for Favored skills. You might want to pick Socialize, since there's a lot of low-Essence Socialize charms for &quot;Blending into the crowd&quot;, and Socialize helps raise your Guile and your Read Intentions rolls for Social Influence.<br /> <br /> Also, might not be worth blowing a Favored on, but Bureaucracy has some great Merchant and buy/sell charms. What good is something stolen if you can't fence it for sweet sweet Jade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T14:11:12-08:00","id":768718,"title":"","content":"Annie are you okay?<br /> Are you okay?<br /> Are you okay, Annie?<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyways, did anyone else feel as though Larceny didn't quite click for them? Especially if you only do the E1 charms. I mean, you get the psuedo-Socialize charm, the gambling charm, and a lockpick charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T01:43:35-08:00","id":769041,"title":"","content":"Wait. Why no Performance Dance Charms?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;From now on, instead of saying 'half-assed', I will use 'muled'. 'This is a muled job, Chris', I will say to my friend Chris. 'You need to do better, or your ass is grass. And not, like, metaphorical grass. There are weeds growing in there as we speak.'<br /> <br /> &quot;'The DEA is after you, man' I will tell him, in all seriousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8891-khantalas","name":"Khantalas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8891_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"899"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-19T14:51:32-08:00","id":769568,"title":"","content":"Going for Performance Acting instead! &quot;Excuse me, I a ma master thespian. Do not disparage my craft you lowly brute! Now let's go steal a theatre.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also yes, lots of Socialize. And some Presence. And yeah, some Bureocracy, because the need to buy some basic supplies (make up, rope aka ancient age duct tape, and normal objects that can substitute as lock picks &lt;_&lt;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1355-horvagab","name":"horvagab","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1355_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}